    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Louise Wang works for a multinational company in Shanghai. One day, she suddenly noticed that something was missing from her office: the familiar clicking sound of "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "high heels",
            "zh": "高跟鞋"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Wang used to wear high heels every day, but she gave them up after a heel got stuck in an "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "air outlet",
            "zh": "出风口"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Now, even colleagues who aren’t very tall no longer wear high heels. And it’s not just in her suburban office. Her company’s other office downtown is seeing the same "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "trend",
            "ref": "v-trend"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Is the age of high heels over? Online shopping platforms may provide some answers. On Taobao, the top 20 best-selling women’s shoes are all "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "flats",
            "zh": "平底鞋"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". The store of Staccato, once known for high heels, now features mostly flats. Their sales are almost 5 times higher than those of heels."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "“This should have happened long ago,” Wang said. “Wearing high heels is like walking on "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "nails",
            "zh": "钉子"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". They are neither comfortable nor "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "practical",
            "ref": "v-practical"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ".”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "For a long time, though, high heels were seen as the height of fashion. In the 20th century, short dresses paired with high heels were a "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "statement",
            "ref": "v-statement"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of freedom and confidence for women. Marilyn Monroe once said, “I don’t know who invented high heels, but all women "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "owe",
            "ref": "v-owe"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " him a lot.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "But doctors have long warned against these shoes. “High heels force women to stand or walk on their tiptoes. Their weight is pushed forward, putting great pressure on their "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "joints",
            "zh": "关节"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and toes,” said Wang Jian, a doctor in Guangzhou."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Women today care more about health and comfort, said fashion brand manager Sissi Gao. This may be why high heels are losing popularity. But will they ever make a comeback? Maybe. “Fashion always changes with the times,” Gao added."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
